# s16_cond_const.tkr — §16 target-conditional const: BOTH `#arch` arms survive under the C-monolith
# backend and codegen emits a C `#if` ladder, so the one `teko.c` cross-compiles across every arch
# (the arm64 first-alloc SIGSEGV fix). The `pick::TAG` reference lowers to the laddered symbol; on the
# x86_64 host the `#if defined(__x86_64__)…` arm selects 64.

Feature: §16 target-conditional const — both arch arms ladder into one teko.c

  Scenario: x86_64_ladder_selects_64 — on x86_64 the #if ladder selects the x86_64 arm, TAG = 64
    When the program is built and run
    Then it exits 64
